Share-alike: because src/spie/conceptnet_data.py is an adaptation of CC BY-SA 4.0
material, any redistribution of that file -- or of data derived from it -- must be
made available under CC BY-SA 4.0 and must carry this attribution.

What was derived, and how: a deterministic offline pipeline reads a pinned ConceptNet
assertions dump, keeps only single-token English terms and the six relation kinds the
engine models (IsA, UsedFor, CapableOf, HasProperty, Causes, PartOf), derives puzzle
affordance tags from a fixed rule table plus IsA inheritance, and retains only those
words that provably invent a formally certified puzzle. No ConceptNet text is
reproduced beyond concept terms and relation labels. The same attribution is embedded
in the generated file itself, as CONCEPTNET_ATTRIBUTION, so it cannot become separated
from the data it covers.

The engine's own hand-curated concept core (the _CONCEPTS literal in
src/spie/concepts.py) is original to this project, is not derived from ConceptNet, and
remains the default vocabulary: the ConceptNet layer is strictly additive and never
overrides a curated concept.
